# Upstream SHAs this suite is proven against.
#
# These live OUTSIDE .github/workflows/ on purpose. GITHUB_TOKEN is not permitted
# to modify workflow files under any permission setting, so while these sat in
# ci.yml the weekly bump job could not propose a change to them -- it failed with
# "refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update workflow ... without
# workflows permission". The alternative was a PAT with `workflow` scope, i.e. a
# new long-lived credential, to edit two hex strings.
#
# Treating the pins as DATA rather than workflow definition is also just truer:
# they describe what was proven, not how to run it. ci.yml loads them; the bump
# job rewrites them.
#
# ENGINE_REF is engine 3.12.0 (felt sidecar + webfetch timeout name).
# FORGE_REF is the join-graph export: world.tscn has no player.gd and no
# world_data, and the engine-lane pack is the 3.12.0 key set. CI regenerates
# fixtures/world.tscn and fixtures/pack.json from this pin. Do not hand-restage.
ENGINE_REF=97d6ef1838aae0218595142a1cb51897776b7b94
FORGE_REF=95917272abf7e2c260f814a855d456ac4eb8cb95
